  "body": "Carries #175 (one NC file per operation, merged into this branch), so this PR closes both #110 and #111. Base is now `main` (its old base #147 has merged), and current main (1da9695) is merged in.\n\n## What changed\n\n**#110: pause or home after an operation, suppress, skip pauses**\n- **After this operation** (per op): Continue (the default), Optional stop, Program stop or Go home. Continue writes nothing, so goldens don't change. Any other choice adds one `PARAM AfterOperation optional-stop|stop|home`. The post writes it after the op's spindle stop:\n  - Fanuc, Haas, Mazak: M1 / M0 / `G91 G28 Z0`, `G28 X0 Y0`, `G90`. On Fanuc, `G49` comes first when TCPM is armed.\n  - Siemens 840D: `G0 G53 Z0`, then XY.\n  - Fanuc Lathe: M01 / M00 / `G28 U0` then `G28 W0`.\n  - Heidenhain: M1 / M0. Go home is refused, naming the op.\n- **`afterModes = true`** (review B2) is a manifest flag, set in the six posts that write `afterOp()`. If a script doesn't declare it, the engine refuses any stop or home ask and names the op: `operation X: asks a program stop after it, but this post script does not declare afterModes ...`. Tormach (new on main) doesn't write after-actions yet, so it refuses the ask instead of running past it.\n- **Suppress** (per op) leaves the op out of the NC and keeps its toolpath. A suppressed stale op doesn't block the post. If every op is suppressed, the post refuses.\n  - New (review B1): `verification_report` refuses when a posted op that reads the program ahead has a suppressed op ahead of it in its setup, and that op cut something: `operation Rest2 was generated against the cut of suppressed Rough1; unsuppress Rough1 or suppress Rest2 too`. Suppressing an op that nothing later depends on still posts.\n- **Skip pauses and homes** is a document switch that removes every after-action. It is undoable.\n\n**#111: one NC file per operation**\n- An Output choice: One program, or One file per operation, written as `<program>_<nn>_<op>.<ext>` into a folder. Each file is a standalone program. Files are written all-or-nothing, and suppressed ops get no file. It now also posts with the document's post options (#34) through `engine::run_numbered_with`.\n\n**Merge with main**\n- Main's `PostOptions` (#34, threading) and this branch's version are merged into one singleton `{ threading, skip_stops, per_op }` with one `SetPostOptions` command. The project reader lands all three fields in one write; before, a second write wiped `threading`.\n- The posts keep main's coolant, wear comp, threading, probe, C-axis live tooling and Tormach changes.\n- Cycle anchors in the combined stream use main's motion count (Move, Touch and Retreat).\n- This branch's RECOMMENDED.md entries moved to `docs/decisions/110-pause-home.md` and `111-nc-per-op.md`. The review-fix decisions are recorded there too.\n\n## Pins\n- `suppressed_rest::suppressing_a_cut_a_later_op_was_generated_against_refuses_by_name` (B1). It checks the combined and per-op posts and the way out.\n- `suppressed_rest::suppressing_an_op_nothing_depends_on_still_posts` (B1)\n- `post_engine::a_stop_asked_of_a_script_without_after_modes_is_refused_by_name` (B2)\n- `after_op` (10), `per_op_files`. `a_suppressed_op_writes_no_file` now suppresses the last op, since suppressing the first one is refused now.\n- ui `after_op_tests`, `state_per_op`\n\n## Readings (worktree, debug, after the merge)\n- camcraft-post: comp 9, post_engine 33. All green.\n- camcraft-app, 66 suites, all green: after_op, per_op_files, suppressed_rest, posting, conformance, golden_cl, fanuc_post, lathe_post (+g76, refusals), tormach_post, coolant(+followups), wear_comp, control_comp, c_axis_live, probe_op, heidenhain_*, commands_undo, project_roundtrip, operations, remachining, setups, scripting, solid_law(+goldens) and every other suite that calls the post gate.\n- ui lib: 282 passed, 2 ignored. No snapshot changes.\n- clippy `-D warnings`: clean on post, app and ui.\n\nChangelog: Pause or home after an operation (optional stop, program stop, go home) in each post's own words; Suppress an operation (refused by name when a later op was generated against its cut); a \"Skip pauses and homes\" post option; and \"One file per operation\" output (#110, #111)\n\nFixes #110\nFixes #111\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
